# Line-ending normalization for the Windows Custom Inventory repo.
#
# Without this, OneDrive and various editors rewrite CRLF<->LF on save and Git
# reports whole files as "modified" even though no content changed. With these
# rules Git stores a normalized LF blob and compares the working tree against
# that normalized form, so end-of-line variations no longer produce diffs.

# Auto-detect text vs binary; store all text normalized to LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# PowerShell scripts: check out with CRLF in the working tree (Windows / PS 5.1
# convention; some 5.1 parsing and signing paths are happiest with CRLF).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Markdown: LF.
*.md  text eol=lf
